          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#in_terms_of_cochains_on_superminkowski_spacetimes"} In terms of cochains on super-Minkowski spacetimes
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#BilinearFierzIdentities"} Bilinear Fierz identities
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#QuadraticFierzIdentities"} Quadrilinear Fierz identities
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            What are called
            %em Fierz identities
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            are the relations that hold between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multilinear+map"} multilinear
            expression in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinors"} spinors
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+spinors"} Majorana spinors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ψ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
            in Lorentzian spacetime dimension 4,5,7,11, then the following identity holds (example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheM2andM5CocyclesAsFierzIdentities"}
            below):
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mover
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo )
                  %mo ∧
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mover
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi b
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\left(\overline{\psi} \wedge \Gamma_{a b} \psi\right)
                  \\wedge
                  \\left(\overline{\psi} \wedge \Gamma^b \psi\right)
                  \\;=\;
                  0
                  \\,.
          %p
            (Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{(-)}
            denotes the Majorana conjugate,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_a
            are a Clifford representations, the “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∧
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge
            ”-signs denotes symmetrization in the spinor components and summation over repeated indices is understood. The details of this are discussed
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "#BilinearFierzIdentities"} below
          %p
            In
            %a{:href => "#DAuriaFreMainaRegge82"} D’Auria-Fré-Maina-Regge 82
            it was pointed out that all Fierz identities may be understood as expressing the product operation in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+ring"} representation ring
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
            (in some given dimension): for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{S_i\}_{i \in I}
            denoting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+representations"} irreducible
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representations"} spin representations
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreps"} irreps
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+representations"} tensor product of representations
            decomposes again as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+representations"} irreducible representations
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi i
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi j
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi k
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S_i \otimes S_j  = \underset{k}{\oplus} C_{i j}{}^k S_k
          %p
            with “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clebsch-Gordan+coefficients"}> Clebsch-Gordan coefficients
            ”
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %msup
                      %mrow
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{i j}{}^k
          %p
            For example for Lorentzian dimension 11 with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 5
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\tfrac{1}{2})^5
            denoting the unique irreducible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+spinor"} Majorana spinor
            representation, then one finds (
            %a{:href => "#DAuriaFre82b"}> D’Auria-Fré 82b, section 3
            ) that the symmetric part in the quadruple tensor product of this representation with itself decomposes as a direct sum of irreps as follows
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mn 2
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mn 5
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mn 2
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mn 5
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mn 2
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mn 5
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mn 2
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mn 5
                      %mo }
                    %mi sym
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 5
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 5
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 4
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 3
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 3
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 3
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 5
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\left\{
                  (\tfrac{1}{2})^5
                  \\otimes
                  (\tfrac{1}{2})^5
                  \\otimes
                  (\tfrac{1}{2})^5
                  \\otimes
                  (\tfrac{1}{2})^5
                  \\right\}_{sym}
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  (0)^5
                  \\;\oplus\;
                  (1)^3 (0)^2
                  \\;\oplus\;
                  (1)^4 (0)
                  \\;\oplus\;
                  (1)^5
                  \\;\oplus\;
                  (2) (0)^4
                  \\;\oplus\;
                  (2)(1)(0)^3
                  \\;\oplus\;
                  (2)^2 (0)^3
                  \\;\oplus\;
                  (2)^2 (1)^3
                  \\;\oplus\;
                  (2)^5
          %p
            where the symbols refer to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Young+diagrams"} Young diagrams
            canonically labeling representations (details are in example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#11dQuadrilinearCGCoefficients"}
            below).
          %p
            The point is that the expression
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mover
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo )
