          #QuadraticFierzIdentitiesIn5d.num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              On D=5
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+of+supersymmetries"} N = 2
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/5d+supergravity"}> 5d supergravity
              ) there are quadrilinear Fierz identities of this form:
            %p
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/FierzIdentitiesForBraneCocyclesIn5d.png", :width => "600"}/
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "#CDF"}> Castellani-D’Auria-Fré 91 (III.5.50)
              ).
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clebsch-Gordan+coefficient"} Clebsch-Gordan coefficient
          %h2#references References
          %p
            Named after
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markus+Fierz"} Markus Fierz
          %p
            The interpretation of Fierz identities as relations satisfied by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clebsch-Gordan+coefficients"} Clebsch-Gordan coefficients
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+ring"} representation ring
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
            originates in
          %ul
            %li#DAuriaFreMainaRegge82
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riccardo+D%27Auria"}> Riccardo D'Auria
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fr%C3%A9"} Pietro Fré
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tullio+Regge"} Tullio Regge
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  A New Group Theoretical Technique for the Analysis of Bianchi Identities and Its Application to the Auxiliary Field Problem of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo =
                        %mn 5
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=5
                  Supergravity
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/0003-4916(82)90007-0"} doi:10.1016/0003-4916(82)90007-0
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/167640"} spire:167640
          %p
            where it was applied to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 4
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(4,1)
            (relevant in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D5+supergravity"} D=5 supergravity
          %p
            By this method the Fierz identities for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spin
